[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066728775","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108561#issuecomment-3066728775","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108561","id":3066728775,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62ypFH","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T08:48:55Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T09:01:37Z","body":"It seems to work (from the disassembly) and can't be any worse than we have now lol. :grin: \r\n\r\nI'm not familiar with `/ENTRY:ShimMainCRTStartup` flags on windows (that could probably do with some explanation in the OP imo, rather than just assuming reader knows...). I'm presuming this is a way of getting it to link / run before everything else.\r\n\r\n> is too primitive to contain any SSE instructions\r\n\r\nThat's a big assumption though.\r\nFrom a quick look the technique may not be completely safe:\r\n\r\n* The `cpp` isn't specifically compiled without the SSE4.2 flags.\r\n* The `cpp` includes `windows.h`, which may in turn depends on runtime libraries which may include SSE4.2 funcs (because of the flags).\r\n\r\nSee https://randomascii.wordpress.com/2016/12/05/vc-archavx-option-unsafe-at-any-speed/ .\r\n\r\nSo as far as I can see it works as compiled above (from the dissassembly) but may not be safe as a general technique for this, in terms of different compiler versions. It may work now, but break in a new compiler / library version, for instance, as there are no guarantees offered here as far as I can see.\r\n\r\nTo do this kind of thing as _safely_ as possible, as I understand it, you need:\r\n* Guarantee to run your cpp code before all else (the technique used here may satisfy this, not sure)\r\n* Compile your cpp explicitly without SSE4.2 flag.\r\n* Not pull in _any_ third party libraries, especially something as large as windows, call CPUID directly, and output an error message using the minimum amount of runtime library requirement.\r\n\r\nN.B. There is I have a feeling some more strict behaviour on MSVC than in other compilers whereby it is easier to exclude instructions from other architectures, but I'm afraid I forgot details. As far as I remember getting gcc / clang to do this correctly on Linux is most difficult.\r\n\r\nIf it helps last time I had a go at this in a module it might give some examples:\r\nhttps://github.com/lawnjelly/godot-lsimd\r\n\r\nBut I can't guarantee that would work in production in the wild, that's only going by the most recent articles I read at the time, and it's a slightly different case as I'm using dynamic dispatch.\r\n\r\nThis is just my understanding, I'm not by any means an expert in this area.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066728775/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066818883","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108561#issuecomment-3066818883","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108561","id":3066818883,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62y_FD","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T09:51:26Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T09:51:26Z","body":"> The cpp isn't specifically compiled without the SSE4.2 flags.\r\n\r\nI guess a flag can be added specifically (changed it to remove SSE4.2 flags for this file), but there is no math in this function, so nothing to optimize using SSE.\r\n\r\n> The cpp includes windows.h, which may in turn depends on runtime libraries which may include SSE4.2 funcs (because of the flags).\r\n\r\nNothing should be executed before the entry point, so it should not matter, `windows.h` is there only to get WinAPI function definitions.\r\n\r\n> Not pull in any third party libraries, especially something as large as windows, call CPUID directly, and output an error message using the minimum amount of runtime library requirement.\r\n\r\nIt's only using Windows system API functions, so it should be completely safe. Using `__cpuid` on the other hand is not safe, it is a CRT function, and CRT is not initialized at this point (and might use SSE code in the init).\r\n\r\nMaking entry point function using x64-64 assembler directly would be absolutely safe, but this seems to be overkill for such minor feature.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066818883/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066820729","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108561#issuecomment-3066820729","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108561","id":3066820729,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62y_h5","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T09:52:59Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T09:52:59Z","body":"> I'm not familiar with /ENTRY:ShimMainCRTStartup flags on windows (that could probably do with some explanation in the OP imo, rather than just assuming reader knows...). I'm presuming this is a way of getting it to link / run before everything else.\r\n\r\nIndeed, it's setting executable entry point, so it will be executed first, before C/C++ runtime init and C++ constructors.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066820729/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066857571","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108561#issuecomment-3066857571","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108561","id":3066857571,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62zIhj","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T10:10:24Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T10:16:49Z","body":"> I guess a flag can be added specifically (changed it to remove SSE4.2 flags for this file), but there is no math in this function, so nothing to optimize using SSE.\r\n\r\nIt's not just math thouh. SSE is often used for e.g. setting memory, string operations etc. Specifically, SSE4.2 introduces PCMPISTRM and PCMPISTRI which are optimized for string and text operations.\r\n\r\nSo even printing a string could invoke SSE4.2.\r\n\r\n> Using __cpuid on the other hand is not safe, it is a CRT function, and CRT is not initialized at this point (and might use SSE code in the init).\r\n\r\nI think it's a CPU instruction afaik.\r\n\r\n> Yes, CPUID is an x86 assembly instruction that retrieves information about the processor, such as its features, manufacturer, model, and supported instruction sets. It is invoked using the CPUID opcode, with specific input values in the EAX register (and sometimes ECX) to determine what information is returned in registers like EAX, EBX, ECX, and EDX.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066857571/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066935875","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108561#issuecomment-3066935875","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108561","id":3066935875,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62zbpD","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T10:36:31Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T10:36:31Z","body":"> I think it's a CPU instruction afaik.\r\n\r\nIf `CPUID` is used as inline assembly, ` __cpuid` is a C runtime built-in function, it is likely using this instruction, but can do something else in its implementation.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066935875/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066951582","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108561#issuecomment-3066951582","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108561","id":3066951582,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62zfee","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T10:41:04Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T10:41:04Z","body":"Is better now it's compiled without SSE4.2 for the file. :+1: \r\n\r\nI do suspect calling CPUID directly would be better, then writing to stdout or something _before_ calling the windows message box (just in case it crashes there), but it's better than nothing now and should catch a lot of cases.\r\n\r\nI guess we'll see in practice whether it still crashes for some people before the message box.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066951582/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066957268","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108561#issuecomment-3066957268","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108561","id":3066957268,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62zg3U","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T10:43:13Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T10:43:13Z","body":"> then writing to stdout or something before calling the windows message box (just in case it crashes there), but it's better than nothing now and should catch a lot of cases.\r\n\r\nWriting to `stdout` probably won't work at all, since CRT is not initialized.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066957268/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066960255","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108561#issuecomment-3066960255","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108561","id":3066960255,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62zhl_","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T10:43:59Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T10:43:59Z","body":"> Writing to stdout probably won't work at all, since CRT is not initialized.\r\n\r\nYeah maybe you are right, I'm not sure how this is usually handled. Either way have approved now. :+1: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066960255/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066970403","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108561#issuecomment-3066970403","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108561","id":3066970403,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62zkEj","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T10:59:19Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T10:59:19Z","body":"> Guarantee to run your cpp code before all else (the technique used here may satisfy this, not sure)\r\n\r\nThis is pretty much impossible to fully guarantee:\r\n- `DLLMain`s can be called before, but Godot is only linked to the system libraries, so it should not be a concern (and we can't do anything with it anyway).\r\n- Native TLS callback can be executed before, but should not do anything before runtime init, only allocates some memory for TLS.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066970403/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3070042218","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108561#issuecomment-3070042218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108561","id":3070042218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62_SBq","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T15:35:07Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T15:35:07Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3070042218/reactions","total_